# Futures Seat-Position Alpha Skill

When the user asks to build or audit futures seat factors, compare seat signals with CTA, check publication lag sensitivity, or reproduce the Q4 seat-signal study, use the local skill package.

Preferred local project path:

```text
.cursor/skills/seat-alpha
```

Workflow:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/seat-alpha/SKILL.md`.
2. For data contracts and baseline files, read `.cursor/skills/seat-alpha/references/data_guide.md`.
3. Use the local `pandadata-api` skill to verify method parameters before any real API call.
4. Set PANDA_DATA_USERNAME and PANDA_DATA_PASSWORD before fetching data, or pass `--data-dir`.
5. Run `scripts/validate.py` before trusting any result; report failures verbatim.
6. Preserve factor definitions, broker lists, execution timing, cost assumptions, and data dates.
7. Do not invent data interfaces, fields, factors, or trading advice.
